WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.680
A cancer treatment plan can change a
person's life.

00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:06.285
But understanding that plan means more
than remembering a medicine's

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:06.700
name.

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:08.720
What is the treatment trying to achieve?

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:11.140
What needs checking before the next cycle?

00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:14.645
Which side effects can be managed at home,
and which need a call

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:15.060
today?

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:18.725
SACTCheck was developed to bring those
questions together, around

00:00:18.740 --> 00:00:20.840
the treatment the person is actually
receiving.

00:00:22.217 --> 00:00:26.322
SACTCheck is a suite of digital oncology
tools that operationalises

00:00:26.337 --> 00:00:29.077
NCCP protocols at the point of care.

00:00:29.597 --> 00:00:33.402
It translates solid-tumour regimen rules,
toxicity thresholds and

00:00:33.417 --> 00:00:36.157
monitoring requirements into structured
digital tools.

00:00:36.797 --> 00:00:40.817
Browse by tumour site, or search by drug,
trade name, indication

00:00:41.057 --> 00:00:42.077
or protocol number.

00:00:42.617 --> 00:00:45.957
Each regimen connects the available
assessment, knowledge, consent,

00:00:46.397 --> 00:00:49.922
supportive care and patient resources,
with links back to the national

00:00:49.937 --> 00:00:50.397
source.

00:00:51.037 --> 00:00:53.177
Coverage and review status remain visible.

00:00:54.825 --> 00:00:59.410
Systemic anti-cancer therapy, or SACT,
includes chemotherapy, hormone

00:00:59.425 --> 00:01:02.285
treatment, targeted medicines and
immunotherapy.

00:01:02.925 --> 00:01:06.325
Antibody-drug conjugates add another layer
of treatment complexity.

00:01:07.085 --> 00:01:10.070
Precision oncology can make the tumour's
biology central to choosing

00:01:10.085 --> 00:01:10.665
a treatment.

00:01:11.165 --> 00:01:14.450
Each approach brings its own schedules,
interactions, monitoring

00:01:14.465 --> 00:01:15.605
needs and risks.

00:01:16.245 --> 00:01:19.550
A general explanation of chemotherapy
cannot answer every question

00:01:19.565 --> 00:01:20.985
about every modern regimen.

00:01:22.753 --> 00:01:25.758
Ireland has national treatment protocols
and valuable information

00:01:25.773 --> 00:01:29.173
from hospitals, the HSE and cancer
charities.

00:01:29.553 --> 00:01:32.718
Yet the practical challenge can be
connecting those resources to

00:01:32.733 --> 00:01:34.513
one person's exact treatment.

00:01:35.253 --> 00:01:38.438
National reviews have long recognised the
need for consistent treatment

00:01:38.453 --> 00:01:40.393
information and documented assessment.

00:01:40.933 --> 00:01:44.138
For patients, information about a drug
alone may not explain the

00:01:44.153 --> 00:01:46.833
combination, the treatment phase or the
next step.

00:01:47.513 --> 00:01:50.778
SACTCheck responds with a dedicated
patient platform connected to

00:01:50.793 --> 00:01:51.653
the clinical regimen.

00:01:53.420 --> 00:01:57.305
Created by Dr Paul O'Brien from his
experience in oncology day-ward

00:01:57.320 --> 00:02:02.120
care, SACTCheck began with a practical
problem: bringing blood results,

00:02:02.580 --> 00:02:06.200
symptoms and treatment rules together in a
clear, repeatable assessment.

00:02:06.860 --> 00:02:10.265
It has grown into a connected platform for
clinicians, patients and

00:02:10.280 --> 00:02:10.700
families.

00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:15.840
The organising principle is the exact
regimen: its indication, medicines,

00:02:16.360 --> 00:02:19.985
schedule and treatment phase, with access
to the official National

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:21.680
Cancer Control Programme source.

00:02:23.207 --> 00:02:26.272
For nursing teams, the clinical decision
tool is designed to support

00:02:26.287 --> 00:02:29.787
structured pre-treatment assessment and
triage for oncology review.

00:02:30.287 --> 00:02:33.932
In this fictional ribociclib example, a
low neutrophil count and

00:02:33.947 --> 00:02:36.227
raised liver enzymes are assessed
separately.

00:02:36.667 --> 00:02:40.487
Each result appears beside its matching
protocol criterion and action,

00:02:40.887 --> 00:02:42.587
making the reason for interruption
visible.

00:02:43.267 --> 00:02:45.067
Missing information remains unassessed.

00:02:45.507 --> 00:02:48.247
That gives the team a clearer basis for
escalation.

00:02:48.607 --> 00:02:52.232
The responsible clinician still makes the
treatment decision; acute

00:02:52.247 --> 00:02:55.507
symptoms follow the service's established
urgent-care pathway.

00:02:57.320 --> 00:03:00.965
The assessment can also produce a copyable
summary and a downloadable

00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:01.560
PDF.

00:03:02.460 --> 00:03:06.145
These bring together the treatment
context, entered findings, relevant

00:03:06.160 --> 00:03:08.560
criteria and any unassessed areas.

00:03:09.280 --> 00:03:12.440
The clinician's decision and rationale are
recorded separately.

00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:17.405
The aim is more consistent documentation
and clearer handover: the

00:03:17.420 --> 00:03:20.865
next person can see the basis of the
assessment, rather than just

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:21.805
a final label.

00:03:21.820 --> 00:03:25.365
Whether that improves documentation
quality and workload needs to

00:03:25.380 --> 00:03:26.320
be measured in practice.

00:03:27.967 --> 00:03:31.432
Alongside the assessment, the knowledge
base brings together why

00:03:31.447 --> 00:03:35.132
a treatment is used, how the medicines
work, the evidence behind

00:03:35.147 --> 00:03:37.507
them and practical monitoring
considerations.

00:03:38.387 --> 00:03:41.792
It helps a clinician move from checking a
rule to understanding the

00:03:41.807 --> 00:03:42.247
treatment.

00:03:43.047 --> 00:03:46.332
Related supportive-care resources,
including anti-sickness guidance

00:03:46.347 --> 00:03:49.987
and draft prescriptions where available,
sit beside that information.

00:03:50.867 --> 00:03:53.812
Source links allow the underlying evidence
to be checked, while the

00:03:53.827 --> 00:03:56.547
individual patient's circumstances remain
central.

00:03:58.367 --> 00:04:00.412
Supportive care belongs beside the
treatment.

00:04:00.427 --> 00:04:04.052
Emetogenic risk describes the chance of
nausea and vomiting.

00:04:04.067 --> 00:04:08.267
Where available, the platform shows that
risk alongside authored,

00:04:08.587 --> 00:04:12.047
phase-specific anti-sickness prescription
drafts, with medicines,

00:04:12.487 --> 00:04:14.007
timing and review prompts.

00:04:14.647 --> 00:04:18.252
Selecting the current phase helps avoid
carrying an old support plan

00:04:18.267 --> 00:04:19.287
into a new treatment.

00:04:19.927 --> 00:04:23.712
Prescriber and pharmacy review remain
essential, including interactions

00:04:23.727 --> 00:04:25.287
and overlapping medicines.

00:04:25.947 --> 00:04:29.872
For ribociclib, heart-rhythm risk means
the anti-sickness plan must

00:04:29.887 --> 00:04:31.007
be chosen individually.

00:04:33.065 --> 00:04:34.725
Consent presents a related challenge.

00:04:35.485 --> 00:04:38.870
Generic templates, particularly older
versions, can require substantial

00:04:38.885 --> 00:04:42.085
additional explanation for newer
treatments and combinations.

00:04:42.965 --> 00:04:46.410
Updating a form helps, but treatment
choices and safety information

00:04:46.425 --> 00:04:47.665
continue to evolve.

00:04:48.145 --> 00:04:51.605
The enduring task is keeping the
discussion specific and current.

00:04:52.345 --> 00:04:56.170
SACTCheck brings treatment explanations
and regimen-specific risk

00:04:56.185 --> 00:04:59.725
information alongside branded
consent-support documents.

00:05:00.485 --> 00:05:03.485
These support discussion of benefits,
risks and alternatives.

00:05:04.205 --> 00:05:07.750
The clinician must personalise and verify
the discussion; generating

00:05:07.765 --> 00:05:10.945
a PDF does not itself establish informed
consent.

00:05:12.558 --> 00:05:15.978
The patient platform carries the same
treatment into everyday language.

00:05:16.438 --> 00:05:19.463
It explains what the medicines are for,
how they are given, what

00:05:19.478 --> 00:05:21.258
a cycle means and what to expect.

00:05:21.898 --> 00:05:25.003
A patient can return to that explanation
at home and share it with

00:05:25.018 --> 00:05:25.443
family.

00:05:25.458 --> 00:05:29.323
Visual information separates common side
effects from warning signs

00:05:29.338 --> 00:05:30.958
that need contact with the team.

00:05:31.338 --> 00:05:34.763
Where a regimen combines different types
of treatment, the explanations

00:05:34.778 --> 00:05:38.983
distinguish their effects rather than
treating every symptom as generic

00:05:38.998 --> 00:05:40.298
chemotherapy toxicity.

00:05:42.118 --> 00:05:44.738
A simple treatment card makes that
connection tangible.

00:05:45.318 --> 00:05:48.783
Patients can print a wallet-sized card
with their regimen, schedule

00:05:48.798 --> 00:05:52.358
and oncology contact details, completed by
their team.

00:05:52.958 --> 00:05:56.718
Its QR code opens the matching treatment
information on a phone.

00:05:57.298 --> 00:06:02.223
At home, on holiday, or abroad, patients
have a practical starting

00:06:02.238 --> 00:06:05.223
point to show another clinician what
treatment they are receiving,

00:06:05.238 --> 00:06:08.438
without relying on memory or finding the
right leaflet.

00:06:09.118 --> 00:06:12.943
On the reverse, a rolling stamp record
lets the team mark completed

00:06:12.958 --> 00:06:15.358
treatment units, with dates and initials.

00:06:15.878 --> 00:06:19.498
This helps keep the conversation anchored
to what was actually completed.

00:06:19.958 --> 00:06:22.098
The card complements the fuller passport.

00:06:22.678 --> 00:06:26.803
The printed details stay to hand; opening
the QR link needs internet

00:06:26.818 --> 00:06:27.418
access.

00:06:29.262 --> 00:06:32.202
The purpose is to equip patients to take
part in their care.

00:06:32.582 --> 00:06:35.542
To understand why blood tests or heart
checks may be needed.

00:06:35.902 --> 00:06:37.842
To recognise symptoms they should report.

00:06:38.142 --> 00:06:41.187
To check with their team before adding
medicines or supplements that

00:06:41.202 --> 00:06:41.982
could affect treatment.

00:06:42.382 --> 00:06:44.562
And to bring better questions to the next
visit.

00:06:45.382 --> 00:06:48.567
Treatment timelines explain phases, breaks
and relevant monitoring

00:06:48.582 --> 00:06:52.207
milestones, helping patients see how
today's appointment fits into

00:06:52.222 --> 00:06:53.122
the wider plan.

00:06:54.695 --> 00:06:58.175
Printable handbooks keep practical advice
available away from a screen.

00:06:58.655 --> 00:07:02.315
A separate Treatment Passport gives
patients space to record symptoms,

00:07:02.735 --> 00:07:06.840
changes and questions cycle by cycle, with
space for clinician grading

00:07:06.855 --> 00:07:07.475
at review.

00:07:08.035 --> 00:07:12.320
Treatment cards and QR links help keep
relevant information and contact

00:07:12.335 --> 00:07:13.495
details accessible.

00:07:14.175 --> 00:07:17.840
The passport supports the next
conversation; urgent symptoms should

00:07:17.855 --> 00:07:20.715
be reported promptly, not saved for the
next appointment.

00:07:21.215 --> 00:07:24.760
Together, these resources connect the
consultation with life between

00:07:24.775 --> 00:07:25.195
visits.

00:07:26.890 --> 00:07:29.870
Keeping pace requires more than publishing
information once.

00:07:30.560 --> 00:07:34.845
SACTCheck includes source links, update
tracking and validation workspaces

00:07:34.860 --> 00:07:37.140
to support review as the platform
develops.

00:07:38.030 --> 00:07:41.795
A sustainability area also explores
evidence and resource considerations

00:07:41.810 --> 00:07:42.910
in treatment delivery.

00:07:43.710 --> 00:07:47.395
Coverage varies by regimen, and
maintaining clinical accuracy requires

00:07:47.410 --> 00:07:49.010
ongoing professional review.

00:07:49.830 --> 00:07:53.295
Patient and public involvement is part of
the next stage: testing

00:07:53.310 --> 00:07:57.335
whether the information is understandable
and useful, alongside evaluation

00:07:57.350 --> 00:07:58.670
of the clinical workflow.

00:08:00.550 --> 00:08:04.455
SACTCheck's purpose is to connect national
guidance, clinical reasoning

00:08:04.470 --> 00:08:07.230
and patient understanding around the same
treatment.

00:08:07.950 --> 00:08:11.990
For teams, a structured way to assess,
explain and document.

00:08:12.770 --> 00:08:16.255
For patients, a clearer account of the
plan and how to participate

00:08:16.270 --> 00:08:16.810
in it.

00:08:17.090 --> 00:08:20.855
It is currently an independent feasibility
evaluation project, with

00:08:20.870 --> 00:08:23.510
clinical and oncology-pharmacy validation
pending.

00:08:24.250 --> 00:08:27.375
The next step is to test these intended
benefits with clinicians

00:08:27.390 --> 00:08:28.330
and patients.

00:08:29.080 --> 00:08:31.780
SACTCheck: from protocol to person.
